---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Methodology & Signal Standards"
  description="How GTAVI.AI scores predictions: confidence tiers, data sources, and editorial standards for GTA VI signal intelligence."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16">

    <div class="mb-10">
      <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-600 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">GTAVI.AI</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Methodology &amp; Signal Standards</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        How we source, score, and present GTA VI intelligence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border-dim overflow-hidden" style="background:var(--c-card)">
        <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-border-dim">
          <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Confidence Scoring</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
            Confidence reflects how many independent signals agree. 80%+ = multiple corroborating data sources. Below 50% = trailer evidence only or high-variance extrapolation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-6 py-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          {[
            { tier: "Confirmed",  range: "90–100%", color: "text-gta-teal",  border: "border-gta-teal/25",  bg: "bg-gta-teal/8",  desc: "Official Rockstar statement, press release, or Rockstar Newswire post." },
            { tier: "Reported",   range: "60–89%",  color: "text-gta-gold",  border: "border-gta-gold/25",  bg: "bg-gta-gold/8",  desc: "Credible journalist sourcing, verified leak, or corroborated community data." },
            { tier: "Predicted",  range: "0–59%",   color: "text-zinc-400",  border: "border-zinc-700",     bg: "bg-zinc-800/50", desc: "Model-derived from historical franchise data. High variance; treat as estimate." },
          ].map(t => (
            <div class={`rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 ${t.border} ${t.bg}`}>
              <div class={`text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest mb-1 ${t.color}`}>{t.tier} · {t.range}</div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">{t.desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border-dim px-6 py-5" style="background:var(--c-card)">
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Data Sources</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
          Release dates from Rockstar announcements. Pricing from CPI-adjusted history. Map and vehicle estimates from trailer analysis and community research.
        </p>
        <a href="/gta-v" class="text-[11px] font-mono text-gta-gold/60 hover:text-gta-gold transition-colors tracking-widest">
          GTA V signal data →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border-dim px-6 py-5" style="background:var(--c-card)">
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Not Official</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
          All predictions are community-derived. GTAVI.AI has no affiliation with Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive. Treat every prediction as informed speculation.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-border-dim">
      <a href="/gta-vi/intel" class="text-[11px] font-mono text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-300 transition-colors tracking-widest uppercase">
        ← Back to GTA VI Intelligence
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>
